@*
	The join-time consent prompt (§5.6).

	Two things this exists to enforce:
	  1. Dismissing is "Not now" — a swipe-away is not consent. The `default off` shape
		 is structural, not a matter of "the switch happens to start off". §5.6 leans on
		 this and §7.3's profile-fields prompt uses the same pattern for the same reason.
	  2. The copy names the wind-down. Through v0.14 the text said flatly "it stops when
		 the ride ends", which the wind-down made untrue — consent copy that overstates
		 the protection is worse than none.

	The parent binds two callbacks: OnShare (yes) and OnDismiss (no / not now). If the
	user closes the modal any other way, the parent should treat it as OnDismiss.
*@

<div class="consent-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="consent-title">
	<div class="consent-card">
		<h2 id="consent-title">Share your location with @RideName?</h2>
		<p>
			Members of <strong>@RideName</strong> will see where you are while the ride is
			live. You can turn this off at any time. It stops when the ride ends — or, if
			the organiser lets riders finish getting home, within two hours of that.
		</p>

		<div class="actions">
			<button type="button" class="primary" @onclick="OnShareAsync">
				Share
			</button>
			<button type="button" @onclick="OnDismissAsync">
				Not now
			</button>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

@code {
	[Parameter, EditorRequired] public string RideName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
	[Parameter] public EventCallback OnShare { get; set; }
	[Parameter] public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }

	private Task OnShareAsync() => OnShare.InvokeAsync();
	private Task OnDismissAsync() => OnDismiss.InvokeAsync();
}

<style>
	.consent-modal {
		position: fixed; inset: 0;
		background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
		display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
		z-index: 1000;
	}
	.consent-card {
		background: white; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;
		max-width: 32rem; width: calc(100vw - 2rem);
	}
	.consent-card h2 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
	.consent-card p { margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.consent-card .actions { justify-content: flex-end; }
	.consent-card button { padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem; }
</style>
